# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "A hash function $H$ can be defined as:\n"
msgstr "Fungsi hash $H$ boleh didefinisikan sebagai:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$H : Σ^* \\rightarrow \\{0,1\\}^n$\n"
msgstr "$H : Σ^* \\rightarrow \\{0,1\\}^n$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $Σ^*$ is the set of all possible strings which we may consider to be "
"binary strings of any length.\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana $Σ^*$ adalah set semua rentetan yang mungkin yang boleh kita anggap "
"sebagai rentetan binari dengan panjang apa pun.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The fact that the size of the input domain $Σ^*$ of $H$ is unbounded while "
"that of the co-domain $\\{0,1\\}^n$ is bounded means that $H$ is necessarily"
" many-to-one mapping infinitely many inputs to any given n-bit string.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fakta bahawa saiz domain input $Σ^*$ bagi $H$ adalah tidak terbatas "
"sementara domain bersama $\\{0,1\\}^n$ adalah terbatas bermakna $H$ "
"semestinya adalah pemetaan banyak-ke-satu yang memetakan infiniti banyak "
"input kepada mana-mana rentetan n-bit yang diberikan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The properties of uniformity and determinism are nicely encapsulated within "
"the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"An idealized cryptographic model often "
"used in theoretical discussions and analyses of cryptographic protocols and "
"schemes, it allows for clear and rigorous analysis of security "
"properties.\">*random oracle model*</DefinitionTooltip> of cryptographic "
"hashing.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sifat keseragaman dan determinisme dirangkum dengan baik dalam "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"An idealized cryptographic model often used "
"in theoretical discussions and analyses of cryptographic protocols and "
"schemes, it allows for clear and rigorous analysis of security "
"properties.\">*model oracle rawak*</DefinitionTooltip> pencincangan "
"kriptografi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Example of cryptographic hashing in Python with SHA-256 {#example-of-"
"cryptographic-hashing-in-python-with-sha-256}"
msgstr ""
"Contoh pencincangan kriptografi dalam Python dengan SHA-256 {#example-of-"
"cryptographic-hashing-in-python-with-sha-256}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This simple example demonstrates cryptographic hashing using the popular [SHA-256](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=SHA-2&oldid=1155462953) algorithm as provided by the `cryptography` Python library.\n"
"First we show how a minor difference in plain texts leads to a very large difference in the hash digests.\n"
msgstr ""
"Contoh mudah ini menunjukkan pencincangan kriptografi menggunakan algoritma [SHA-256](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=SHA-2&oldid=1155462953) yang popular seperti yang disediakan oleh pustaka Python `cryptography`.\n"
"Pertama, kita tunjukkan bagaimana perbezaan kecil dalam teks biasa membawa kepada perbezaan yang sangat besar dalam digest hash.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The two messages differ in exactly one character.\n"
msgstr "Kedua-dua mesej berbeza dalam tepat satu aksara.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we instantiate `hash` objects to enable the hashing process, which "
"involves calls to two methods: `update` and `finalize`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seterusnya, kita instantiasikan objek `hash` untuk membolehkan proses "
"pencincangan, yang melibatkan panggilan kepada dua kaedah: `update` dan "
"`finalize`.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We see that due to the avalanche effect in the SHA-256 CHF, a one-character "
"difference in input messages yields two very different digests.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita lihat bahawa disebabkan kesan avalans dalam SHA-256 CHF, perbezaan satu"
" aksara dalam mesej input menghasilkan dua digest yang sangat berbeza.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Applications of cryptographic hashing {#applications-of-cryptographic-"
"hashing}"
msgstr ""
"Aplikasi pencincangan kriptografi {#applications-of-cryptographic-hashing}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The unique properties of CHFs make them suitable for a wide array of "
"applications:\n"
msgstr "Sifat unik CHF menjadikannya sesuai untuk pelbagai aplikasi:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Data integrity checks:** Hash functions can be used to create a "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Commonly used technique in cryptography to "
"detect errors during data transmission involving adding a value(which is "
"often derived from the data itself) to the data to create a checksum value. "
"The recipient can then perform the same calculation to compare checksums to "
"verify authenticity.\">checksum</DefinitionTooltip> for a set of data. Any "
"modifications to the data, intentional or not, will result in a different "
"checksum, alerting systems or users to the change. The checksum is also "
"typically much more compact than the original data, which makes checksum "
"comparisons very fast.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Semakan integriti data:** Fungsi hash boleh digunakan untuk mencipta "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Commonly used technique in cryptography to "
"detect errors during data transmission involving adding a value(which is "
"often derived from the data itself) to the data to create a checksum value. "
"The recipient can then perform the same calculation to compare checksums to "
"verify authenticity.\">checksum</DefinitionTooltip> bagi set data. Sebarang "
"pengubahsuaian pada data, sama ada disengajakan atau tidak, akan "
"menghasilkan checksum yang berbeza, memberitahu sistem atau pengguna tentang"
" perubahan tersebut. Checksum biasanya juga jauh lebih padat daripada data "
"asal, menjadikan perbandingan checksum sangat pantas.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Fig 1: Secure hashing for data integrity "
"checks](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/cryptographic-"
