msgid "*Figure 1. Secure hashing for data integrity*\n"
msgstr "*Rajah 1. Pencincangan selamat untuk semakan integriti data*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Digital signatures:** Cryptographic hashes are essential to the "
"functioning of digital signatures as they involve comparing "
"cryptographically hashed messages to establish authenticity and integrity "
"while preserving privacy.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Tandatangan digital:** Hash kriptografi adalah penting untuk fungsi "
"tandatangan digital kerana ia melibatkan perbandingan mesej yang dicincang "
"secara kriptografi untuk membuktikan keaslian dan integriti sambil "
"mengekalkan privasi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Fig 2: Digital signatures](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-"
"cryptography/cryptographic-hash-functions/digital-signature.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Fig 2: Digital signatures](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-"
"cryptography/cryptographic-hash-functions/digital-signature.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Figure 2. Digital signatures*\n"
msgstr "*Rajah 2. Tandatangan digital*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Blockchain and cryptocurrencies:** Cryptocurrencies like Bitcoin rely "
"heavily on CHFs, particularly in creating transaction integrity and enabling"
" consensus mechanisms like *proof of work*.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Blockchain dan mata wang kripto:** Mata wang kripto seperti Bitcoin "
"bergantung banyak pada CHF, terutamanya dalam mewujudkan integriti transaksi"
" dan membolehkan mekanisme konsensus seperti *bukti kerja*.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Security of cryptographic hashing {#security-of-cryptographic-hashing}"
msgstr ""
"Keselamatan pencincangan kriptografi {#security-of-cryptographic-hashing}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The security of a CHF is typically assessed based on resistance to two types"
" of attacks: [pre-"
"image](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Preimage_attack&oldid=1145879411)"
" and "
"[collision](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Collision_attack&oldid=1138239916).\n"
msgstr ""
"Keselamatan sebuah CHF biasanya dinilai berdasarkan rintangan terhadap dua "
"jenis serangan: [pra-"
"imej](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Preimage_attack&oldid=1145879411)"
" dan "
"[perlanggaran](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Collision_attack&oldid=1138239916).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Pre-image resistance {#pre-image-resistance}"
msgstr "Rintangan pra-imej {#pre-image-resistance}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Pre-image resistance* means that given a digest, it should be infeasible to"
" find the input.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Rintangan pra-imej* bermakna bahawa diberikan sebuah digest, adalah tidak "
"dapat dilaksanakan secara praktikal untuk mencari input.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This is related to the one-way property of CHFs.\n"
msgstr "Ini berkaitan dengan sifat sehala CHF.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A good CHF is designed in such a way that a party wishing to conduct a pre-"
"image attack has no better option than a brute force approach, which has "
"time complexity $2^n$.\n"
msgstr ""
"CHF yang baik direka bentuk sedemikian rupa sehingga pihak yang ingin "
"melakukan serangan pra-imej tidak mempunyai pilihan yang lebih baik daripada"
" pendekatan brute force, yang mempunyai kerumitan masa $2^n$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: <Accordion>
# <AccordionItem title="<em>mathematical details</
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<AccordionItem title=\"<em>Mathematical details</em>\">\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given a CHF $H$ and digest $g$, it should be computationally infeasible to "
"find any input $m$ from the pre-image of $g$ whereby $H(m) = g$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Diberikan CHF $H$ dan digest $g$, adalah tidak mungkin secara pengiraan "
"untuk mencari sebarang input $m$ daripada pra-imej $g$ di mana $H(m) = g$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Collision resistance {#collision-resistance}"
msgstr "Rintangan perlanggaran {#collision-resistance}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Collision resistance* means that it is difficult to find two different "
"inputs that hash to the same digest.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Rintangan perlanggaran* bermakna adalah sukar untuk mencari dua input "
"berbeza yang menghasilkan digest yang sama.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A *cryptographic hash collision* occurs when two inputs hash to the same "
"digest. While collisions inevitably exist given the many-to-one nature of "
"CHFs, a good CHF nevertheless makes it infeasible to locate one at will.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Perlanggaran hash kriptografi* berlaku apabila dua input menghasilkan "
"digest yang sama. Walaupun perlanggaran tidak dapat dielakkan memandangkan "
"sifat banyak-ke-satu CHF, CHF yang baik tetap menjadikannya tidak dapat "
"dilaksanakan secara praktikal untuk mencari satu secara sesuka hati.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Collision resistance is crucial for applications like digital signatures and"
" certificates, where it could be disastrous if a malicious party were able "
"to create a forgery that hashes to the same value.\n"
msgstr ""
"Rintangan perlanggaran adalah penting untuk aplikasi seperti tandatangan "
"digital dan sijil, di mana ia akan menjadi bencana jika pihak berniat jahat "
"mampu mencipta pemalsuan yang menghasilkan hash kepada nilai yang sama.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: <Accordion>
# <AccordionItem title="<em>mathematical details o
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<AccordionItem title=\"<em>Mathematical details of hash collisions</em>\">\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid " $m_1, m_2$ can be found such that $H(m_1) = H(m_2)$.\n"
msgstr " $m_1, m_2$ boleh ditemui sedemikian sehingga $H(m_1) = H(m_2)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Hash length {#hash-length}"
msgstr "Panjang hash {#hash-length}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Collision resistance is a harder requirement than pre-image resistance and "
"necessitates output lengths twice as long as that needed for pre-image "
"resistance. This is because a brute force attack known as the [birthday "
"attack](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Birthday_attack&oldid=1161075943),"
" which can be used to identify hash collisions, has time complexity "
"$2^{n/2}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Rintangan perlanggaran adalah keperluan yang lebih keras daripada rintangan "
"pra-imej dan memerlukan panjang output dua kali lebih panjang daripada yang "
"diperlukan untuk rintangan pra-imej. Ini kerana serangan brute force yang "
"dikenali sebagai [serangan hari "
"lahir](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Birthday_attack&oldid=1161075943),"
" yang boleh digunakan untuk mengenal pasti perlanggaran hash, mempunyai "
"kerumitan masa $2^{n/2}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the absence of cryptanalytic weaknesses, the security of a hash function "
"is therefore primarily influenced by its hash length. The longer the hash, "
"the more secure it is, as it becomes harder to mount brute force attacks.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tanpa kelemahan kriptanalisis, keselamatan fungsi hash oleh itu terutamanya "
"dipengaruhi oleh panjang hashnya. Semakin panjang hash, semakin selamat ia, "
"kerana serangan brute force menjadi semakin sukar.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Commonly used cryptographic hash functions {#commonly-used-cryptographic-"
"hash-functions}"
msgstr ""
"Fungsi hash kriptografi yang biasa digunakan {#commonly-used-cryptographic-"
"hash-functions}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following table lists some commonly used cryptographic hash functions, "
"along with their hash lengths and primary application domains:\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadual berikut menyenaraikan beberapa fungsi hash kriptografi yang biasa "
"digunakan, bersama panjang hash dan domain aplikasi utama mereka:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Hash Function | Output Length (bits) | Common Applications                                        |\n"
"|---------------|----------------------|------------------------------------------------------------|\n"
"| MD5           | 128                  | File integrity checking, older systems, non-crypto uses    |\n"
"| SHA-1         | 160                  | Legacy systems, Git for version control                    |\n"
"| SHA-256       | 256                  | Cryptocurrency (Bitcoin), digital signatures, certificates |\n"
"| SHA-3         | Variable (up to 512) | Various cryptographic applications, successor to SHA-2     |\n"
"| Blake2        | Variable (up to 512) | Cryptography, replacing MD5/SHA-1 in some systems          |\n"
"| Blake3        | Variable (up to 256) | Cryptography, file hashing, data integrity                 |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Fungsi Hash | Panjang Output (bit) | Aplikasi Biasa                                             |\n"
"|-------------|----------------------|------------------------------------------------------------|\n"
"| MD5         | 128                  | Semakan integriti fail, sistem lama, kegunaan bukan kripto |\n"
"| SHA-1       | 160                  | Sistem lama, Git untuk kawalan versi                       |\n"
"| SHA-256     | 256                  | Mata wang kripto (Bitcoin), tandatangan digital, sijil     |\n"
"| SHA-3       | Boleh ubah (hingga 512) | Pelbagai aplikasi kriptografi, pengganti SHA-2          |\n"
"| Blake2      | Boleh ubah (hingga 512) | Kriptografi, menggantikan MD5/SHA-1 dalam sesetengah sistem |\n"
"| Blake3      | Boleh ubah (hingga 256) | Kriptografi, pencincangan fail, integriti data           |\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- [MD5](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=MD5&oldid=1161719955) and [SHA-1](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=SHA-1&oldid=1161401043), while still seen in less sensitive applications places, are considered deprecated in terms of collision resistance and are not recommended for new systems.\n"
"SHA-256, part of the [SHA-2](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=SHA-2&oldid=1155462953) family, is widely used and currently secure for most applications.\n"
"- [SHA-3](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=SHA-3&oldid=1161463128) is a newer standard that was selected by NIST in 2015 as the winner of the NIST hash function competition. It's designed to be a drop-in replacement for SHA-2, but it also has some different internal characteristics and is resistant to certain types of attacks that might be effective against SHA-2.\n"
"- [Blake2 and Blake3](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=BLAKE_(hash_function)&oldid=1161463384) are cryptographic hash functions that are faster than MD5, SHA-1, SHA-2, and SHA-3, but at least as secure as the latest standard, SHA-3. They are increasingly being used in new systems, particularly where speed is important.\n"
msgstr ""
"- [MD5](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=MD5&oldid=1161719955) dan [SHA-1](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=SHA-1&oldid=1161401043), walaupun masih digunakan dalam aplikasi yang kurang sensitif, dianggap lapuk dari segi rintangan perlanggaran dan tidak disyorkan untuk sistem baru.\n"
"SHA-256, sebahagian daripada keluarga [SHA-2](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=SHA-2&oldid=1155462953), digunakan secara meluas dan kini selamat untuk kebanyakan aplikasi.\n"
"- [SHA-3](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=SHA-3&oldid=1161463128) adalah standard yang lebih baharu yang dipilih oleh NIST pada tahun 2015 sebagai pemenang pertandingan fungsi hash NIST. Ia direka bentuk sebagai pengganti langsung untuk SHA-2, tetapi ia juga mempunyai beberapa ciri dalaman yang berbeza dan tahan terhadap jenis serangan tertentu yang mungkin berkesan terhadap SHA-2.\n"
"- [Blake2 dan Blake3](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=BLAKE_(hash_function)&oldid=1161463384) adalah fungsi hash kriptografi yang lebih pantas daripada MD5, SHA-1, SHA-2, dan SHA-3, tetapi sekurang-kurangnya selamat seperti standard terkini, SHA-3. Mereka semakin banyak digunakan dalam sistem baru, terutamanya di mana kelajuan adalah penting.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum risks to traditional cryptographic hashing {#quantum-risks-to-"
"traditional-cryptographic-hashing}"
msgstr ""
"Risiko kuantum terhadap pencincangan kriptografi tradisional {#quantum-"
"risks-to-traditional-cryptographic-hashing}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The primary quantum threat to cryptographic hashing is posed by brute force "
"attacks.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ancaman kuantum utama terhadap pencincangan kriptografi ditimbulkan oleh "
"serangan brute force.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given a particular digest, an attacker will try out random inputs until they"
" locate one which produces the same digest.\n"
msgstr ""
"Diberikan digest tertentu, penyerang akan mencuba input rawak sehingga "
"menemui satu yang menghasilkan digest yang sama.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With $n$ bits in the input, there are $2^n$ possible values. Therefore, the "
"attacker needs to try out around $2^{n-1}$ inputs to have a better than 50% "
"chance of success.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan $n$ bit dalam input, terdapat $2^n$ nilai yang mungkin. Oleh itu, "
"penyerang perlu mencuba sekitar $2^{n-1}$ input untuk mempunyai peluang "
"kejayaan lebih daripada 50%.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Grover's algorithm {#grovers-algorithm}"
msgstr "Algoritma Grover {#grovers-algorithm}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For such an unstructured search context, Grover's algorithm can provide a "
"quadratic speedup using a technique known as <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Technique used in algorithms to leverage certain phenomenons in"
" the quantum interface which increase the probability (amplitude) of the "
"correct answer when searching through a large set of "
"possibilities/definitions.\">quantum amplitude "
"amplification</DefinitionTooltip>, reducing the time complexity of a pre-"
"image attack to $2^{n/2}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk konteks carian tidak berstruktur seperti ini, algoritma Grover boleh "
"memberikan percepatan kuadratik menggunakan teknik yang dikenali sebagai "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Technique used in algorithms to leverage "
"certain phenomenons in the quantum interface which increase the probability "
"(amplitude) of the correct answer when searching through a large set of "
"possibilities/definitions.\">amplifikasi amplitud "
"kuantum</DefinitionTooltip>, mengurangkan kerumitan masa serangan pra-imej "
"kepada $2^{n/2}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In practical terms, this means that a 256-bit CHF, which is currently "
"considered secure against pre-image attacks by classical computers, would "
"provide the same level of security as a 128-bit CHF when faced with a "
"quantum attacker utilizing Grover's algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam istilah praktikal, ini bermakna CHF 256-bit, yang kini dianggap "
"selamat terhadap serangan pra-imej oleh komputer klasik, akan memberikan "
"tahap keselamatan yang sama seperti CHF 128-bit apabila berhadapan dengan "
"penyerang kuantum yang menggunakan algoritma Grover.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Grover's algorithm by itself is not known to provide additional quantum "
"speedups with respect to collision attacks beyond the limit set by the "
"[birthday "
"attack](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Birthday_attack&oldid=1161075943),"
" which can be carried out on classical computers. Since the classical "
"birthday attack already requires CHFs to employ hash lengths that are twice "
"as long as needed for pre-image resistance, the fact that Grover search "
"effectively halves the hash length with respect to pre-image attacks does "
"not pose a practical threat.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma Grover dengan sendirinya tidak diketahui memberikan percepatan "
"kuantum tambahan berkenaan serangan perlanggaran melebihi had yang "
"ditetapkan oleh [serangan hari "
"lahir](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Birthday_attack&oldid=1161075943),"
" yang boleh dijalankan pada komputer klasik. Oleh kerana serangan hari lahir"
" klasik sudah memerlukan CHF menggunakan panjang hash yang dua kali lebih "
"panjang daripada yang diperlukan untuk rintangan pra-imej, fakta bahawa "
"carian Grover secara efektif mengurangkan separuh panjang hash berkenaan "
"serangan pra-imej tidak menimbulkan ancaman praktikal.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, in the case of SHA-256, performing on the order of $2^{128}$ "
"operations to execute a Grover-assisted pre-image attack would still be "
"infeasible in the foreseeable future.\n"
msgstr ""
"Contohnya, dalam kes SHA-256, melaksanakan sekitar $2^{128}$ operasi untuk "
"melakukan serangan pra-imej berbantuan Grover masih tidak mungkin dilakukan "
"dalam masa terdekat.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "BHT algorithm {#bht-algorithm}"
msgstr "Algoritma BHT {#bht-algorithm}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A quantum algorithm that combines aspects of the birthday attack with Grover"
" search was proposed in 1997 by [Brassard, Høyer, and "
"Tapp](http://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/9705002) (BHT) and affords a theoretical"
" scaling of $O(2^{n/3})$ for finding hash collisions. However, this improved"
" scaling is predicated on the existence of quantum random access memory "
"[QRAM](http://arxiv.org/abs/2205.14023) technology, which currently does not"
" exist.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma kuantum yang menggabungkan aspek serangan hari lahir dengan carian"
" Grover dicadangkan pada tahun 1997 oleh [Brassard, Høyer, dan "
"Tapp](http://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/9705002) (BHT) dan memberikan penskalaan"
" teori $O(2^{n/3})$ untuk mencari perlanggaran hash. Walau bagaimanapun, "
"penskalaan yang lebih baik ini bergantung pada kewujudan teknologi memori "
"akses rawak kuantum [QRAM](http://arxiv.org/abs/2205.14023), yang kini tidak"
" wujud.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Without QRAM, the realizable scaling is $\\tilde{O}(2^{2n/5})$ and for hash "
"lengths currently in use, this marginal improvement in collision-finding "
"capability relative to the birthday attack does not represent a critical "
"threat.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tanpa QRAM, penskalaan yang boleh dicapai adalah $\\tilde{O}(2^{2n/5})$ dan "
"untuk panjang hash yang kini digunakan, penambahbaikan marginal dalam "
"keupayaan mencari perlanggaran berbanding serangan hari lahir ini tidak "
"mewakili ancaman kritikal.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Summary {#summary}"
msgstr "Ringkasan {#summary}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Cryptographic hash functions are an essential component for ensuring data "
"integrity and privacy in digital information systems and find widespread "
"application in many contexts.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fungsi hash kriptografi adalah komponen penting untuk memastikan integriti "
"dan privasi data dalam sistem maklumat digital dan digunakan secara meluas "
"dalam banyak konteks.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The security requirements of CHFs are mainly understood in terms of their "
"resistance to pre-image and collision attacks. For well-designed CHFs, the "
"hash length is a good proxy for the security level.\n"
msgstr ""
"Keperluan keselamatan CHF terutamanya difahami dari segi rintangan mereka "
"terhadap serangan pra-imej dan perlanggaran. Untuk CHF yang direka bentuk "
"dengan baik, panjang hash adalah proksi yang baik untuk tahap keselamatan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While the advent of quantum computers executing the Grover and BHT "
"algorithms in theory affects the pre-image and collision resistance of "
"traditional CHFs, the long hash lengths already in use today means that "
"modern cryptographic hashing algorithms, such as SHA-3, are likely to remain"
" secure barring the discovery of as-yet-unknown cryptanalytic attacks.\n"
msgstr ""
"Walaupun kemunculan komputer kuantum yang melaksanakan algoritma Grover dan "
"BHT secara teori mempengaruhi rintangan pra-imej dan perlanggaran CHF "
"tradisional, panjang hash yang panjang yang sudah digunakan hari ini "
"bermakna algoritma pencincangan kriptografi moden, seperti SHA-3, "
"berkemungkinan kekal selamat kecuali ditemui serangan kriptanalisis yang "
"belum diketahui.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The relevance of CHFs lies in their role as a fundamental building block for"
" quantum-resistant cryptographic schemes, ensuring that digital information "
"remains secure even in the face of potential future advancements in quantum "
"computing algorithms and technologies.\n"
msgstr ""
"Relevansi CHF terletak pada peranannya sebagai blok binaan asas untuk skim "
"kriptografi tahan kuantum, memastikan maklumat digital kekal selamat "
"walaupun berhadapan dengan potensi kemajuan masa depan dalam algoritma dan "
"teknologi pengkomputeran kuantum.\n"
